    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "A couple took out a six-year loan to start a business. For the first three years, compound interest of 8% p.a. was charged. For the second three years, compound interest of 12% p.a. was charged. Find the total percentage increase in the amount owing. Give your answer to 2 decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "76.98% increase.\n\nMultiply the growth factors for the two three-year periods.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\text{Overall multiplier}&=(1.08)^3(1.12)^3\\\\\\text{Percentage increase}&=[(1.08)^3(1.12)^3-1]\\times100\\%\\\\\\text{Percentage increase}&\\approx76.98\\%\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
